Negative control for the editor's boot step when it is handed a record id
(R-EDIT-HANDOFF, RT2).

An editor opened with `recordId` edits an EXISTING record: it boots
`.withId(recordId)` and titles as an update. `isNew` is what decides between
that and `.fresh()`. This mutant lets `isNew` read the context alone, so a
handoff that names only a record id is taken for a new draft: the dialog boots
`.fresh()`, the id is never applied, and the title says "Add New".

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Expected red (component lane): manage-dialog-fresh-boot.spec.ts — an editor
opened with a `recordId` and no context must take `.withId(recordId)` and never
`.fresh()`.

